Conflicts: cupsomatic-ppd (<< 20030507), hpijs (<< 2)
Filename: pool/main/f/foomatic-filters-ppds/foomatic-filters-ppds_20080528-2.1_all.deb
Size: 3383120
MD5sum: 3a6bb7b1743d9fb76c2a14e3c0ba6c38
SHA1: 48640d5bfdfd9c0f7e3b102a456e42f5c514d54a
SHA256: cc97905d40cbf17e66fcfd6d1183b1a1bb6c30f1c0759c0ce7b883a6c4ca296e
Description: OpenPrinting printer support - prebuilt PPD files
 Foomatic is a printer database designed to make it easier to set up
 common printers for use with Debian (and other operating systems).
 It provides the "glue" between a print spooler (like CUPS or lpr) and
 your actual printer, by telling your computer how to process files
 sent to the printer.
 .
 This package provides Adobe-compliant PPD files for *every single
 printer* supported by Foomatic.  Unless you want to be able to select
 your printer from the web interface of CUPS or PPR, you almost
 certainly don't want this package.  Instead, you can use the
 "foomatic-configure" script in foomatic-db-engine, the "foomatic-gui"
 package, or the web interface for getting a particular PPD file at
 http://www.openprinting.org/printer_list.cgi
 .
 This package *does not* provide manufacturer-supported PPD files for
 PostScript printers; those are included in the openprinting-ppds
 package.
Homepage: http://www.openprinting.org/
Tag: hardware::printer, role::app-data, use::driver, use::printing, works-with::text, works-with-format::pdf
Task: desktop, print-server

