Description: GNOME interface to peercast
 Geekast is an alternative to the Web interface.
 Currently, it can perform audio (Ogg and MP3) or video (OGM) streaming
 through an external player like totem, or an internal player based on
 the Gstreamer multimedia framework.
 In the future, it should be possible to encode a Webcam or any input
 stream over the peercast network.
 .
 This meta-package provides all needed software for running geekast over
 a peercast-servent on localhost. For more customised installation, use
 peercast-geekast and geekast-binary separately.
