SHA256: 3ea19d191b25f6457a6b1e0730a5ae73ae50398e7b037c98b8822beb796838eb
Description: scripts for dynamic IP to name mappings
 GnuDIP is a service designed for an ISP to give its customers a static DNS
 name without having to give them their own IP address. For those who are
 familiar with ml.org this is a simple replacement.
 .
 GnuDIP has two main parts on the server side. 1, the multi-threaded
 server that listens on a port 3495 that accepts connections from client
 applications and updates their hostname, and 2 the web cgi that is used
 as the administration tool and as the users tool to manage their own
 account.
 .
 Using the web cgi a user can set their desired homepage in their settings
 and then set the special URL as the default page for their browser so now
 every time they open their browser their hostname will be automatically
 updated without having to run any other sort of client application and then
 they would be redirected to the URL they set in their GnuDIP settings.
Tag: implemented-in::perl, interface::daemon, network::server, protocol::dns, protocol::http, role::program, web::cgi

