Description: Pixbuf-based theme engine for GTK+ 2.x
 Sapwood is a pixbuf-based 'theme' that allows you to configure the look of
 GTK-using programs. The programs need no modifications to use themes; the
 support is built into GTK+.
 .
 The engine is similar to the pixbuf engine, but uses client-server design
 and pixmaps rather than pixbufs. It is faster and more memory efficient than
 the pixbuf engine, but doesn't do scaling or gradients.
Original-Maintainer: Tommi Komulainen <tommi.komulainen@nokia.com>
Tag: uitoolkit::gtk

