Priority: optional
Section: perl
Installed-Size: 332
Maintainer: Ivan Kohler <ivan-debian@420.am>
Architecture: all
Version: 0.005-3
Depends: libauthen-dechpwd-perl (>= 2.002-3), libcrypt-blowfish-perl (>= 2.0), libcrypt-des-perl, libcrypt-eksblowfish-perl (>= 0.003-3), libcrypt-mysql-perl, libcrypt-passwdmd5-perl (>= 1.0), libcrypt-unixcrypt-xs-perl, libdata-entropy-perl, libdigest-md4-perl (>= 1.2), libdigest-perl (>= 1.0), libdigest-sha1-perl, libmodule-runtime-perl, libparams-classify-perl, perl (>= 5.6.0-16)
Filename: pool/main/liba/libauthen-passphrase-perl/libauthen-passphrase-perl_0.005-3_all.deb
Size: 102606
MD5sum: 6c9c7925cbd37b733f3a0f9f29bf68a7
SHA1: 99df98745ba4c9bc3dd05a912272cdcc8d8f6617
SHA256: 972ae8044a382c31714c6cbb5ab1658cdfece82c343ff2a499534c5aef32be88
Description: Perl module encapsulating hashed passwords/passphrases as objects
 This is the base class for a system of objects that encapsulate
 passphrases.  An object of this type is a passphrase recogniser: its
 job is to recognise whether an offered passphrase is the right one.
 For security, such passphrase recognisers usually do not themselves know
 the passphrase they are looking for; they can merely recognise it when
 they see it.  There are many schemes in use to achieve this effect,
 and the intent of this class is to provide a consistent interface to
 them all, hiding the details.
 .
 This package contains implementations of several specific passphrase schemes
 in addition to the base class.

