Description: Haskell library for building Internet applications
 HAppS is a Haskell library for building Internet applications.
 .
 This library allows writing web services using an elegant monadic
 framework for managing control-flow within the server. Built-in proxy
 functionality can be used to let ajax apps easily access the data
 they need anywhere on the internet.
 .
 Hello world can be as simple as:
  import HAppS.Server
  main = simpleHTTP nullConf [ method GET $ ok "Hello World" ]
