Package: msntp
Priority: optional
Section: net
Installed-Size: 100
Maintainer: Adam Cécile (Le_Vert) <gandalf@le-vert.net>
Architecture: i386
Version: 1.6.dfsg-2
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.3.6-6)
Filename: pool/main/m/msntp/msntp_1.6.dfsg-2_i386.deb
Size: 37324
MD5sum: d4432916836e196c99fe731597dfdde4
SHA1: ae65609768b3dc238aedaf80327668d259316342
SHA256: 438e3926adc28d17b26c7ce5110efee6dd82bfa89f332710b03744c4d8c35b78
Description: A very simple and portable SNTP client/server
 MSNTP is intended to be a straightforward SNTP (Simple Network Time Protocol)
 daemon/utility that is easy to build on any reasonable Unix platform (and most
 near-Unix ones), whether or not it has ever been ported to them before. It is
 intended to answer the following requirements, either by challenge and
 response or the less reliable broadcast method:
 .
 A simple command to run on Unix systems that will check the time and
 optionally drift compared with a known, local and reliable NTP time server.
 No privilege is required just to read the time and estimate the drift.
 .
 A client for Unix systems that will synchronise the time from a known, local
 and reliable NTP time server.
 .
 A server for Unix systems that are synchronised other than by NTP methods and
 that need to synchronise other systems by NTP. It is NOT intended to work as a
 peer with true NTP servers, and won't.
 .
 Homepage: http://www.hpcf.cam.ac.uk/export/
Tag: network::client, network::server, role::program, use::timekeeping

