SHA256: 67d634d8b5e306db448d80d9f9b9c870359c1162839cc7d573044ab15eadf028
Description: useful tool for manipulating PDF documents
 If PDF is electronic paper, then pdftk is an electronic stapler-remover,
 hole-punch, binder, secret-decoder-ring, and X-Ray-glasses. Pdftk is a
 simple tool for doing everyday things with PDF documents. Keep one in the
 top drawer of your desktop and use it to:
  - Merge PDF documents
  - Split PDF pages into a new document
  - Decrypt input as necessary (password required)
  - Encrypt output as desired
  - Fill PDF Forms with FDF Data and/or Flatten Forms
  - Apply a Background Watermark
  - Report PDF on metrics, including metadata and bookmarks
  - Update PDF Metadata
  - Attach Files to PDF Pages or the PDF Document
  - Unpack PDF Attachments
  - Burst a PDF document into single pages
  - Uncompress and re-compress page streams
  - Repair corrupted PDF (where possible)
 .
  Author: Sid Steward <ssteward@accesspdf.com>
Homepage: http://www.pdfhacks.com/pdftk/
Tag: implemented-in::c++, implemented-in::java, interface::commandline, role::program, scope::utility, security::cryptography, use::converting, works-with::text, works-with-format::pdf

