Package: pidgin-otr
Priority: optional
Section: net
Installed-Size: 116
Maintainer: Thibaut VARENE <varenet@debian.org>
Architecture: i386
Version: 3.2.0-2
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.7-1), libgcrypt11 (>= 1.4.0), libotr2 (>= 3.2.0), pidgin (<< 3.0), pidgin (>= 2.4)
Filename: pool/main/p/pidgin-otr/pidgin-otr_3.2.0-2_i386.deb
Size: 52266
MD5sum: 8b8fb65b95f9fda0ce710d44be8654a1
SHA1: a444bf62c52b9ebff324366bdef4e950b0f2b23b
SHA256: a769f17dbc0bbb97b298d00a33861411f49a31e3b05f9898029ef846f9f28a6a
Description: Off-the-Record Messaging plugin for pidgin
 Off-the-Record (OTR) Messaging plugin for pidgin
 .
 OTR allows you to have private conversations over IM by providing:
  - Encryption
    - No one else can read your instant messages.
  - Authentication
    - You are assured the correspondent is who you think it is.
  - Deniability
    - The messages you send do _not_ have digital signatures that are
      checkable by a third party.  Anyone can forge messages after a
      conversation to make them look like they came from you.  However,
      _during_ a conversation, your correspondent is assured the messages
      he sees are authentic and unmodified.
  - Perfect forward secrecy
    - If you lose control of your private keys, no previous conversation
      is compromised.
 .
 This is a pidgin plugin which implements Off-the-Record (OTR) Messaging.
Tag: implemented-in::c, interface::x11, protocol::{jabber,msn-messenger,yahoo-messenger}, role::plugin, security::{authentication,cryptography,privacy}, uitoolkit::gtk, use::chatting

