 Powertweak is a tool for tweaking Linux systems to peak performance.  It
 can be used to tune PCI devices and kernel parameters to use optimal
 settings and enables performance enhancing features of the CPU(s).  To
 use all of powertweak's features you need to be running a Linux kernel
 which supports the /proc/bus/pci and /dev/cpu/<n> interfaces.
 .
