SHA256: 2bf64cc0638b30eb35617bbc83c6a90a37950b444a8dd96889b4b5b12ad1b009
Description: Bittorrent client based on libtorrent-rasterbar with a nice Qt4 GUI
 qBittorrent is a feature rich bittorrent client written in C++ and Qt4 which
 is based on libtorrent-rasterbar. It can be considered as a good alternative
 to other clients. Most important features are:
 .
  * UPnP / NAT-PMP port forwarding support
  * Encryption support (compatible with Azureus)
  * Download from RSS streams
  * An integrated search engine
  * DHT (trackerless) support
  * uTorrent Peer eXchange support (PeX)
  * Directory scanning with automated download of torrents inside
  * Good internationalization (~25 languages supported)
  * Media File previewing while downloading
  * Torrent trackers edition and prioritizing
  * Styles support
  * Files prioritizing in a torrent
  * Tracker authentication support
  * Unicode support
  * Torrent downloading directly from their url
  * Connection though a proxy
  * IP Filtering similar to the one in eMule
Homepage: http://www.qbittorrent.org/
Tag: implemented-in::c++, interface::x11, network::client, protocol::bittorrent, role::program, uitoolkit::qt, use::downloading, x11::application

