Architecture: i386
Source: linux-modules-extra-2.6 (2.6.26-6)
Version: 2:2.6.26-6
Depends: squashfs-modules-2.6.26-1-486, linux-latest-modules-2.6.26-1-486
Filename: pool/main/l/linux-modules-extra-2.6/squashfs-modules-2.6-486_2.6.26-6_i386.deb
Size: 4558
MD5sum: 6a81ff7bd68f68056ad51f8790ff60a6
SHA1: 79dec8230297e79013a38dc1661719d8722e4713
SHA256: fb9463e96d9169cdf595c98fcbf6cfecbc029196b0d16328bae4dc40972aa827
Description: Compression filesystem for Linux 2.6 on x86
 This package depends on the Compression filesystem modules for latest
 Linux kernel 2.6 on x86 and compatible machines.
 .
 Squashfs is a highly compressed read-only filesystem for Linux.  It uses
 zlib compression to compress both files, inodes and directories.  Inodes
 in the system are very small and all blocks are packed to minimise data
 overhead.  Block sizes greater than 4K are supported up to a maximum of
 64K.
 .
 Squashfs is intended for general read-only filesystem use, for archival
 use (i.e.  in cases where a .tar.gz  file may be used), and in constrained
 block device/memory systems (e.g.  embedded systems) where low overhead is
 needed.
Tag: admin::filesystem, admin::kernel, implemented-in::c, role::dummy

