Package: unperish
Priority: optional
Section: devel
Installed-Size: 220
Maintainer: Lars Wirzenius <liw@liw.fi>
Architecture: all
Version: 2.7-1
Depends: python, python-central (>= 0.6.7)
Recommends: bzr, dpkg-dev, lintian, pbuilder, piuparts, reprepro, devscripts, gnupg, sudo
Filename: pool/main/u/unperish/unperish_2.7-1_all.deb
Size: 29984
MD5sum: 8f18149fb5074b6c45d78cce4e567ddf
SHA1: 4fca5e6f542b807d7eac8d583003628cbd82762b
SHA256: d3f71ef4edfa1bf29cf6fb5b8811376f831719d7ddd0608ce6dbc7416845e303
Description: release and build free software projects
 Unperish takes care of all the repetitive, mechanical steps of
 releasing and building a free software project. Starting from files
 committed to a version control system (Bazaar, for now), with a
 single command it can create the upstream tarball (foo-1.2.tar.gz) and
 the Debian source package (.orig.tar.gz, .dsc, .diff.gz), then build
 the binary package using pbuilder, check the result with lintian
 and piuparts, and put the results in an apt repository using
 reprepro (assuming everything is OK). Any step or steps can be done
 individually as well. Further, it is built around a plugin
 architecture, making automation of additional steps easy.
Homepage: http://liw.iki.fi/liw/unperish/
Python-Version: all

