Filename: pool/main/v/vamp-plugin-sdk/vamp-examples_1.2-1.1_i386.deb
Size: 120436
MD5sum: 0e918dc84772c49edac02a18c9f099ff
SHA1: 4ca2f40ae8a976ad0d41bcd43d0098ef90067763
SHA256: 01618a66098f901c4bd5d087c855f9cd54f2cb0654557e1bbd3a93b10fcb6d64
Description: example Vamp plugins and host
 Vamp is an audio processing plugin system for plugins that extract
 descriptive information from audio data - typically referred to as
 audio analysis plugins or audio feature extraction plugins.
 .
 This package contains the following example plugins:
 .
  * ZeroCrossing: calculates the positions and density of
    zero-crossing points in an audio waveform.
 .
  * SpectralCentroid: calculates the centre of gravity of the
    frequency domain representation of each block of audio.
 .
  * AmplitudeFollower is an implementation of SuperCollider's
    amplitude-follower algorithm as a simple Vamp plugin.
 .
  * PercussionOnsetDetector estimates the locations of percussive
    onsets using a simple method described in "Drum Source Separation
    using Percussive Feature Detection and Spectral Modulation" by Dan
    Barry, Derry Fitzgerald, Eugene Coyle and Bob Lawlor, ISSC 2005.
 .
 Also included is a simple host that can enumerate plugins, list their
 features, and process an audio file.

Package: vamp-plugin-sdk
Priority: extra
Section: sound
Installed-Size: 4612
Maintainer: Székelyi Szabolcs <cc@mail.3d.hu>
