Package: wapiti
Priority: optional
Section: python
Installed-Size: 144
Maintainer: Thomas Bläsing <thomasbl@pool.math.tu-berlin.de>
Architecture: all
Version: 1.1.6-3
Depends: python (>= 2.4), python-central (>= 0.6.6)
Recommends: python-utidylib (>= 0.2), python-ctypes (>= 1.0.1)
Filename: pool/main/w/wapiti/wapiti_1.1.6-3_all.deb
Size: 18702
MD5sum: f4c69539b868aafe2e5a9583abc95985
SHA1: 81334fed107680aa90045e82416d65cee3bdd0cd
SHA256: 9d2745e57acb4fe989c0f706c3ea2f496ebd98372055f1c2094592ab37917e34
Description: Web application vulnerability scanner
 Wapiti allows you to audit the security of your web applications.
 It performs "black-box" scans, i.e. it does not study the source code of the
 application but will scans the web pages of the deployed web applications,
 looking for scripts and forms where it can inject data.
 Once it gets this list, Wapiti acts like a fuzzer, injecting payloads to see
 if a script is vulnerable.
 Wapiti can detect the following vulnerabilities:
    - File Handling Errors (Local and remote include/require, fopen, ...)
    - Database Injection (PHP/JSP/ASP SQL Injections and XPath Injections)
    - XSS (Cross Site Scripting) Injection
    - LDAP Injection
    - Command Execution detection (eval(), system(), passtru()...)
    - CRLF Injection (HTTP Response Splitting, session fixation...)
Homepage: http://wapiti.sourceforge.net/
Python-Version: >= 2.4

